    "title": "FEMA Sends Florida $317 Million as Jacksonville Hospital, Cape Coral Canals Get Fixes - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Quin Marlowe ,\n9 hours ago FEMA has approved $317 million in disaster recovery and hazard-mitigation funding for Florida, with nearly $53 million of it earmarked for St. Vincent's Medical Center Riverside in Jacksonville to armor the hospital's roof, walls and other building components against hurricane-force winds and flooding. The money spans projects from home elevations to canal debris removal, touching hospitals, utilities, parks and electrical systems across the state. Read full article\n6",
